          "page_text": "NVIDIA Number of Employees 2026 | Employee Count & Headcount Data | Revelio Labs\nSolutions\nIntelligence Platform\nData\nCompany Benchmarking\nCompensation Data\nLocation Strategy\nTalent Intelligence\nCompany Discovery\nTalent Solutions\nData Enrichment\nTalent Acquisition\nProducts\nExplore Products\nTerminal\nNEW\nCOSMOS\nConsulting\nData Builder\nJob Architecture\nReports\nAcademic Research\nNewsroom\nExplore Newsroom\nLatest Articles\nRevelio Public Labor Statistics\nAI Labor Market Tracker\nNEW\nAcademic Publications\nCompany\nExplore Company\nAbout Us\nCareers\nEvents\nPodcast\nTalk to an Expert\nResources\nExplore Resources\nData Dictionary\nCompany Directory\nPress\nBlog\nFAQ\nSign In\nSign Out\nTalk to an Expert\nOpen Terminal\nCompanies\nNVIDIA Corp.\nEmployees\nNASDAQ: NVDA\nHow many employees work at\nNVIDIA\n?\nNVIDIA Corp.\n(NVDA)\nhas approximately\n44,949\ntotal employees worldwide as of\nMarch 2026\n, according to Revelio Labs workforce intelligence data.\nNVIDIA\n’s total headcount has\ngrown\n36.2%\nfrom 33,004 employees in 2023 to 44,949 in 2026\n.\nData source: Revelio Labs\n•\nCoverage: Global workforce,\n2023\n–\n2026\n•\nPublished\nAugust 2026\nIs\nNVIDIA\nhiring right now?\nYes\n,\nNVIDIA\nis\nactively\nhiring.\nNVIDIA\nhad\n7,177\nactive job postings in\n2026\n, a\n132.9\n%\nincrease\nfrom\n2025\n—\nsee job openings & hiring trends\n.\nAbout\nNVIDIA\n’s Workforce\nNVIDIA Corp.\n(\nNVDA\n)\nis an Electronics Manufacturing company that employs\n44,949\npeople worldwide as of March\n2026\n. It is the 5th-largest by headcount among its\npeers\n. Founded in\n1993\n, the company is headquartered in Santa Clara, California and trades on the NASDAQ.\nNVIDIA's workforce has grown\n36.2%\nfrom\n2023\nto\n2026\n, up\n2.5%\nyear over year in\n2026\n. Its workforce is concentrated most in North America (\n55.0%\n), followed by South Asia (\n18.3%\n) and East Asia (\n11.0%\n).\nNVIDIA's functional groups are Finance and Operations (\n37.5%\n), Engineering (\n37.1%\n), and Sales and Marketing (\n25.3%\n), with Sales and Marketing growing fastest (up\n7.0%\n). The average salary is\n$163,787,\nranging from a median of\n$213,000\nin North America to\n$39,000\nin South Asia, down\n2.4%\nyear over year in\n2026\n.\nNVIDIA's active job postings rose\n132.9%\nin\n2026\nto\n7,177\n, with new postings per month climbing from\n1,694\nin\n2023\nto\n3,840\nin\n2026\n. Overall employee sentiment is positive and broadly stable.\nSourced from Revelio Labs workforce data.\nTicker\nNASDAQ: NVDA\nHeadquarters\nSanta Clara, California\nFounded\n1993\nIndustry\nElectronics Manufacturing\nEmployees\n44,949\nYoY\n+2.5% (+6,311)\nAs of\nMarch 2026\nNVIDIA\nworkforce metrics\nHeadcount\n44.9k\n▲\n2.5% YoY\nAvg. Salary\n$163.8k\n▼\n2.4% YoY\nGrowth Rate\n2.5%\n▲\n1.4pts YoY\nTenure\n0.0yr\nUnlock Metrics\nHiring Rate\n00.0%\nUnlock Metrics\nAttrition Rate\n00.0%\nUnlock Metrics\nUnlock hiring rate, attrition rate, and 12 additional workforce metrics for\nNVIDIA\n.\nCompare to peers, export the dataset, and access the full quarterly history.\nUnlock Metrics\nNVIDIA Annual Employee Count (2023-2026)\nInteractive chart of\nNVIDIA\nannual worldwide employee count from\n2023\nto\n2026\n.\nNVIDIA\nhad\n44,949\nemployees in\n2026\n, a\n2.5\n%\nincrease\n(\n+\n6,311\n)\nfrom\n2025\n.\nNVIDIA\nhad\n42,903\nemployees in\n2025\n, a\n1.8\n%\nincrease\n(\n+\n4,985\n)\nfrom\n2024\n.\nNVIDIA\nhad\n37,918\nemployees in\n2024\n, a\n1.4\n%\nincrease\n(\n+\n3,471\n)\nfrom\n2023\n.\nNVIDIA\nhad\n34,447\nemployees in\n2023\n, a\n0.5\n%\nincrease\n(\n+\n1,588\n)\nfrom\n2022\n.\nNVIDIA's total workforce has grown from\n33,004\nemployees in\n2023\nto\n44,949\nin\n2026\n.\nNVIDIA Corp. quarterly employee count\nYear\nQtr\nEmployees\nYoY Change\nYoY %\n2026\nQ1\n44,949\n+6,311\n+2.5%\n2025\nQ4\n42,903\n+4,985\n+1.8%\n2025\nQ3\n41,145\n+4,055\n+1.4%\n2025\nQ2\n40,090\n+3,263\n+0.9%\n2025\nQ1\n38,638\n+3,332\n+1.1%\n2024\nQ4\n37,918\n+3,471\n+1.4%\n2024\nQ3\n37,090\n+3,582\n+1.9%\n2024\nQ2\n36,827\n+3,823\n+2.4%\n2024\nQ1\n35,306\n+2,654\n+1.3%\n2023\nQ4\n34,447\n+1,588\n+0.5%\n2023\nQ3\n33,508\n+702\n-0.2%\n2023\nQ2\n33,004\n-236\n-1.1%\nSee NVIDIA's complete headcount history, including quarterly breakdowns.\nGet the Data\nNVIDIA Employee Count by Region (2026)\nNorth America accounts for the largest share of NVIDIA's global workforce with approximately\n55%\nof total employees, followed by South Asia and East Asia.\nNVIDIA employees by region\nRegion\nEmployees\n% of Total\nNorth America\n24,388\n55.0%\nSouth Asia\n8,122\n18.3%\nEast Asia\n4,878\n11.0%\nCentral and Western Asia\n3,533\n8.0%\nWestern Europe\n1,176\n2.7%\nNorthern Europe\n725\n1.6%\nSoutheast Asia\n431\n1.0%\nEastern Europe\n357\n0.8%\nArab States\n203\n0.5%\nSouthern Europe\n155\n0.4%\nDrill into city-level data, hiring trends by region, and historic geographic shifts.\nUnlock Geographic Data\nNVIDIA Employee Count by Department (2026)\nNVIDIA's employee groups are Finance and Operations (\n37.5%\n), Engineering (\n37.1%\n), and Sales and Marketing (\n25.3%\n).\nNVIDIA employees by department\nDepartment\nEmployees\n% of Total\nFinance and Operations\n16,856\n37.5%\nEngineering\n16,669\n37.1%\nSales and Marketing\n11,372\n25.3%\nCompare NVIDIA's department mix to industry peers.\nSee Full Data\nNVIDIA Employee Salary by Region (2026)\nNVIDIA's average employee salary is\n$163,787\nglobally. Employees in North America receive the highest compensation, with median pay approximately\n1\n.3x the global average. Pay is lowest in South Asia, at a median of\n$39,000\n.\nNVIDIA median employee salary by region (USD)\nRegion\nMedian Salary\nNorth America\n$213,000\nPacific Islands\n$179,000\nNorthern Europe\n$170,000\nWestern Europe\n$158,000\nCentral and Western Asia\n$134,000\nSouthern Europe\n$98,000\nEast Asia\n$79,000\nEastern Europe\n$78,000\nCentral America and the Caribbean\n$56,000\nSoutheast Asia\n$48,000\nArab States\n$45,000\nSouth Asia\n$39,000\nSouth America\n$37,000\nNorth Africa\n$23,000\nSub-Saharan Africa\n$18,000\nUnlock salary by role, level, and city — and compare to NVIDIA's industry peers.\nUnlock Salary Data\nNVIDIA Job Openings and Hiring Trends (2023-2026)\nInteractive chart of\nNVIDIA\nannual active job postings from\n2023\nto\n2026\n.\nNVIDIA\nhad\n7,177\nactive job postings in\n2026\n, a\n132.9\n%\nincrease\n(\n+\n736\n)\nfrom\n2025\n.\nNVIDIA\nhad\n6,441\nactive job postings in\n2025\n, a\n85.3\n%\nincrease\n(\n+\n3,851\n)\nfrom\n2024\n.\nNVIDIA\nhad\n2,590\nactive job postings in\n2024\n, a\n3.3\n%\ndecline\n(\n-\n87\n)\nfrom\n2023\n.\nNVIDIA\nhad\n2,677\nactive job postings in\n2023\n, a\n62.4\n%\nincrease\nfrom\n2022\n.\nHiring velocity\nin\n2026\n:\n3,840\nnew roles/month\n,\nup\nfrom\n1,860\nin\n2025\nand\n1,876\nin\n2024\n.\nNVIDIA's hiring is accelerating: active job postings rose\n132.9%\nin\n2026\nto\n7,177\n, with new postings per month climbing from\n1,694\nin\n2023\nto\n3,840\nin\n2026\n.\nTrack new postings per month, role-level demand, and hiring velocity vs. peers.\nUnlock Hiring Data\nNVIDIA Employee Sentiment (2026)\nRevelio Labs tracks employee sentiment across NVIDIA's workforce based on public professional data. Overall sentiment is positive and has held steady year over year in\n2026\n.\nOverall\nNegative\nPositive\nUnlock the full sentiment breakdown\nby department, tenure, and trend over time.\nUnlock Sentiment\nSimilar Companies\nSimilar\nElectronics Manufacturing\nCompanies by Employee Count\nIntel Corp.\n88,861\nBroadcom Inc.\n37,112\nQUALCOMM, Inc.\n53,972\nMicron Technology, Inc.\n54,818\nRenesas Electronics Corp.\n21,809\nInventec Corp.\n28,714\nQuanta Computer, Inc.\n59,986\nKeysight Technologies, Inc.\n17,011\nAdvanced Micro Devices, Inc.\n31,832\nCadence Design Systems, Inc.\n14,598\nFrequently Asked Questions About NVIDIA\nHow fast is NVIDIA growing?\nIn\n2026\n, NVIDIA's headcount grew\n2.5%\nto\n44,949\nemployees, up from\n38,638\nin\n2025\n.\nSee the full headcount history\nWhere are NVIDIA employees located?\nMost NVIDIA employees are based in North America (\n55.0%\nof headcount), followed by South Asia and East Asia.\nExplore where the workforce is based\nWhat is the average salary at NVIDIA?\nThe average employee salary at NVIDIA is approximately\n$163.8\nk per year.\nAnalyze the salary distribution\nHow many new job postings does NVIDIA open per year?\nIn Q1\n2026\n, NVIDIA opened\n11,519\nnew job postings. In\n2025\n, NVIDIA opened\n22,318\nnew job postings — about\n1,860\nper month.\nTrack hiring trends by role\nWhen was NVIDIA founded and where is it headquartered?\nNVIDIA was founded in\n1993\nand is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.\nCompare NVIDIA to industry peers\nSpeak with a workforce expert about\nNVIDIA\n.\nBook a Demo\nSee something that doesn't look right?\nReach out\nand our team will review it.\nContents\nWorkforce Overview\nWorkforce Metrics\nAnnual Employee Count\nEmployee Count by Region\nEmployee Count by Department\nEmployee Salary by Region\nJob Openings and Hiring Trends\nEmployee Sentiment\nSimilar Companies (Competitors)\nFrequently Asked Questions\nWant even more\nNVIDIA\nworkforce intelligence and insights?\nBook a Demo\nUnderstand the workforce\nWe’re hiring!\nSolutions\nData\nCompany Benchmarking\nCompensation Data\nLocation Strategy\nTalent Intelligence\nCompany Discovery\nData Enrichment\nTalent Acquisition\nGet Started\nTalk to an Expert\nStart Free Trial\nSign In\nSign Out\nProducts\nTerminal\nCOSMOS\nConsulting\nData Builder\nJob Architecture\nReports\nAcademic Research\nCompany\nAbout Us\nCareers\nEvents\nPodcasts\nResources\nData Dictionary\nCompany Directory\nJob Board\nPricing\nPress\nBlog\nFAQ\nNewsroom\nLatest Articles\nRevelio Public Labor Statistics\nAI Labor Market Tracker\nAcademic Publications\nLegal & Privacy\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms of Service\nDo Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\nCPRA Privacy Notice\nVDPA\nGDPR Privacy Notice\nCooki