          "source_url": "https://www.intc.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/1635/intel-accelerates-ai-development-with-reference-kits",
          "publisher": "www.intc.com",
          "extracted_fact": "**Why It Matters:** Built on the [oneAPI](https://www.oneapi.io/) open, standards-based, heterogeneous programming model and components of Intel’s end-to-end AI software portfolio, such as [Intel® AI Analytics Toolkit](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/tools/oneapi/ai-analytics-toolkit.html) and the [Intel® Distribution of OpenVINO™ toolkit](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/tools/openvino-toolkit/overview.html), the reference kits enable AI developers to streamli",
          "excerpt": "Intel offers a set of 34 open source AI reference kits that enable developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments. (Credit: Intel Corporation) [...] Intel offers a set of 34 open source AI reference kits that enable developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments. (Credit: Intel Corporation) [...] # Intel Corporation\n\n# Press Releases\n\n# Intel Accelerates AI Development with Reference Kits\n\nIntel offers a set of 34 open source AI reference kits that enable developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments. (Credit: Intel Corporation)\n# [Intel Corporation](/)\n\n# Press Releases\n\n# Intel Accelerates AI Development with Reference Kit",
          "page_text": "Intel offers a set of 34 open source AI reference kits that enable developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments. (Credit: Intel Corporation) [...] Intel offers a set of 34 open source AI reference kits that enable developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments. (Credit: Intel Corporation) [...] # Intel Corporation\n\n# Press Releases\n\n# Intel Accelerates AI Development with Reference Kits\n\nIntel offers a set of 34 open source AI reference kits that enable developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments. (Credit: Intel Corporation)\n# [Intel Corporation](/)\n\n# Press Releases\n\n# Intel Accelerates AI Development with Reference Kits\n\n![Intel offers a set of 34 open source AI reference kits that enable developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments. (Credit: Intel Corporation)](https://d1io3yog0oux5.cloudfront.net/_3ccf9cf30376bf77bbb27f582e51d00d/intel/news/1635/8284/image.jpeg)\n\nIntel offers a set of 34 open source AI reference kits that enable developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments. (Credit: Intel Corporation)\n\n[Download as PDF](https://d1io3yog0oux5.cloudfront.net/_3ccf9cf30376bf77bbb27f582e51d00d/intel/news/2023-07-24_Intel_Accelerates_AI_Development_with_Reference_1635.pdf \"PDF: Intel Accelerates AI Development with Reference Kits\")\n\n**Optimized AI reference kits help developers and data scientists innovate faster.**\n\nSANTA CLARA, Calif.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- **What's New:** Intel now offers a set of 34 open source [AI reference kits](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/topic-technology/artificial-intelligence/reference-kit.htm) to the community, the result of a [yearslong collaboration](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/newsroom/news/intel-releases-open-source-ai-reference-kits.html) with Accenture, enabling developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments.\n\nThis press release features multimedia. View the full release here: <https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20230724121115/en/>\n\n![Intel offers a set of 34 open source AI reference kits that enable developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments. (Credit: Intel Corporation)](https://mms.businesswire.com/media/20230724121115/en/1847586/4/newsroom-reference-kit-infographic.jpg)\n\nIntel offers a set of 34 open source AI reference kits that enable developers and data scientists to deploy artificial intelligence (AI) faster and more easily. Each kit includes model code, training data, instructions for the machine learning pipeline, libraries and oneAPI components to optimize AI and make it accessible to organizations in multiarchitecture on-premises, cloud and edge environments. (Credit: Intel Corporation)\n\n*“Intel AI reference kits give millions of developers and data scientists an easy, performant and cost-effective way to build and scale their AI applications in health and life sciences, financial services, manufacturing, retail and many other domains. Intel is committed to enabling an AI everywhere future through not just our portfolio of AI-accelerated processors and systems but also our contributions to an open AI software ecosystem. The reference kits are built using components of Intel’s AI software portfolio and on the foundation of the open, standards-based, oneAPI multiarchitecture programming model.”*–Wei Li, Ph.D., Intel vice president and general manager of AI and Analytics\n\n**Why It Matters:** Built on the [oneAPI](https://www.oneapi.io/) open, standards-based, heterogeneous programming model and components of Intel’s end-to-end AI software portfolio, such as [Intel® AI Analytics Toolkit](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/tools/oneapi/ai-analytics-toolkit.html) and the [Intel® Distribution of OpenVINO™ toolkit](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/tools/openvino-toolkit/overview.html), the reference kits enable AI developers to streamline the process of introducing AI into their applications, enhancing existing intelligent solutions and accelerating deployment. The result is proven performan",
