          "publisher": "www.broadcom.com",
          "extracted_fact": "Broadcom has the hardware, firmware, and software for a variety of networking solutions that can be included in the XPU as plug-and-play chiplets. [Skip to main content](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/ai-infrastructure/innovations-in-ai-infrastructure-building-custom-ai-accelerators#content)[](https://www.broadcom.com/home)[Newsroom](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news)",
          "excerpt": "#### The Broadcom Advantage\n\nBroadcom is committed to building on its decade-long industry leadership in custom silicon. We know what custom silicon builds require. That is why we have such a large and proactive investment in R&D – about $3 billion annually -- in creating technology of the future. The vast majority of this investment is prioritized for the AI market.\n\nFor example, our Co Package Optics Cores (proven in our latest XPU) can save 80 watts of system power per XPU. Imagine the benefits of putting a million of these accelerators together with that power and cost savings.\n\nWe continue to lead in areas such as high speed SERDES, chip to chip connectivity, high speed memory, 2.5 and 3D packaging, and time to market, at an annual cadence or faster, depending on customer needs. [...] Our accumulated knowledge over the last decade of co-developing XPUs uniquely positions us to quickly assist our customers. For example, we have finessed the mechanical, thermal, and electrical flows, and fine-tuned our testing and automation to streamline design and development.\n\nBroadcom has the hardware, firmware, and software for a variety of networking solutions that can be included in the XPU as plug-and-play chiplets. This allows our customers to emulate, simulate, and take the accelerator to production faster and more efficiently.\n\nSumming it up: Our Custom XPU engagement model allows our partners to get the best quality, performance, and TCO tuned for their workloads.\n\n#### The Bro",
          "page_text": "#### The Broadcom Advantage\n\nBroadcom is committed to building on its decade-long industry leadership in custom silicon. We know what custom silicon builds require. That is why we have such a large and proactive investment in R&D – about $3 billion annually -- in creating technology of the future. The vast majority of this investment is prioritized for the AI market.\n\nFor example, our Co Package Optics Cores (proven in our latest XPU) can save 80 watts of system power per XPU. Imagine the benefits of putting a million of these accelerators together with that power and cost savings.\n\nWe continue to lead in areas such as high speed SERDES, chip to chip connectivity, high speed memory, 2.5 and 3D packaging, and time to market, at an annual cadence or faster, depending on customer needs. [...] Our accumulated knowledge over the last decade of co-developing XPUs uniquely positions us to quickly assist our customers. For example, we have finessed the mechanical, thermal, and electrical flows, and fine-tuned our testing and automation to streamline design and development.\n\nBroadcom has the hardware, firmware, and software for a variety of networking solutions that can be included in the XPU as plug-and-play chiplets. This allows our customers to emulate, simulate, and take the accelerator to production faster and more efficiently.\n\nSumming it up: Our Custom XPU engagement model allows our partners to get the best quality, performance, and TCO tuned for their workloads.\n\n#### The Broadcom Advantage [...] At Broadcom, we work with our customers to customize their architecture so they can maximize the performance of their AI infrastructure and internal workloads. Optimizing hardware also leads to a smaller, less expensive, and reduced footprint. Customers that engage with us to co-develop these custom chips tend to save billions of dollars of capital expenses because they are designed to perform exactly as planned, with the right ratio of accelerator, memory bandwidth, and I/O bandwidth. Optimizing the hardware for AI infrastructure also means lowering the power and, therefore, the overall cost of these custom chips.\n\nTaken together, these advantages combine to make Custom XPUs the ideal financial and engineering solution for consumer AI.\n\n#### The Broadcom Engagement Model\nMenu\n\n[Skip to main content](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/ai-infrastructure/innovations-in-ai-infrastructure-building-custom-ai-accelerators#content)[](https://www.broadcom.com/home)[Newsroom](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news)\n\nAmericas – English\n\nSelect your region\n\nAmericas Europe, the Middle East and Africa Asia Pacific\n\nSelect language\n\n[English](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news)\n\n*   News Releases  \n*   Articles  \n*   Media Resources  \n\n[Subscribe](https://engage.broadcom.com/newsroom-subscribe)\n\nAmericas – English\n\nSelect your region\n\nAmericas\n\n[English](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news)\n\nEurope, the Middle East and Africa\n\n[EMEA (English)](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/emea)[Español](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/es)[Français](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/fr)[Deutsch](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/de)[Italiano](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/it)\n\nAsia Pacific\n\n[APJ (English)](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/apj)[简体中文](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/cn)[日本語](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/jp)[한국어](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/kr)\n\n Back\n\n[All News Releases](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/releases)\n\nNews Releases\n\n[Product Releases](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/releases?tab=products)[Financial Releases](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/releases?tab=financial)\n\n[All News Releases](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/releases)\n\n Back\n\n[All Articles](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles)\n\nArticles\n\nAI\n\n[AI Infrastructure](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/ai-infrastructure)[Edge AI](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/edge-ai)[Generative AI](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?subCategory[]=Generative%20AI)[Networking for AI](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/networking-for-ai)\n\n[Cloud](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/cloud)[Kubernetes](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?subCategory[]=Kubernetes)[Private Cloud](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?subCategory[]=Private%20Cloud)[Sovereign Cloud](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/sovereign-cloud)\n\nIndustry\n\n[Automotive](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?industry[]=Automotive)[Broadband](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?industry[]=Broadband)[Financial Services](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?industry[]=Financial%20Services)[Government](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/government)[Wireless](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/wireless)\n\n[Networking](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/networking)[Ethernet](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?subCategory[]=Ethernet)[Networking Standards](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?subCategory[]=Networking%20Standards)[Power Efficiency](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?subCategory[]=Power%20Efficiency)\n\n[Security](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/security)[Application Security](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?subCategory[]=Application%20Security)[Cloud Security](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?subCategory[]=Cloud%20Security)[Data Security](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?subCategory[]=Data%20Security)[Network Security](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles?subCategory[]=Network%20Security)\n\n[All Articles](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles)\n\nSeries\n\n[CEO Insights](https://www.broadcom.com/company/news/articles/