          "excerpt": "Amantya Technologies was founded in 2018 by Anuradha Gupta and Sanjay Bisen and is headquartered in Gurugram, Haryana, India, with offices in Bengaluru, Nagpur, the United States, the United Kingdom, and Canada. The company is privately held and operates as a product engineering and systems integration firm specializing in 5G, IoT, AI, edge computing, and cloud solutions. Amantya has expanded into GCC enablement services, offering AI-powered Global Capability Center solutions that combine pre-trained talent, AI-enabled accelerators, and end-to-end engineering services. The company GCC framework is built on intelligent automation, orchestration, and AI agent-driven delivery. Amantya offers three engagement models for GCCs: Build-Operate-Transfer where the company designs staffs and operates the GCC end-to-end before transitioning to full client ownership; Managed Services where Amantya takes full ownership of defined functions combining AI accelerators and expert squads; and Staff Augmentation providing skilled engineers and domain experts on demand. The company AI solutions include AI Code Transformation, AI Log Analyzer, Autonomous Network Suite, and DevOps and Infrastructure AI. Amantya serves tier-1 operators, enterprises, OEMs, and system integrators across telecommunications, technology, and manufacturing industries. The company employs approximately 558 to 746 people globally with the majority based in India. Annual revenue is estimated between 50 million and 100 million dollars with the Indian entity reporting 124 crore Indian rupees for the fiscal year ending March 2024. Amantya has received the Bharat Telecom Export Excellence Award 2025, Globalisation Excellence Award 2025, and Best AI for Telecommunications at the Entrepreneur India AI Awards Summit 2025. Leadership is headed by Founder and CEO Anuradha Gupta with Co-founder and CTO Sanjay Bisen.\nAlgomine was founded in 2015 and is headquartered in Warsaw, Mazowieckie, Poland. The company is part of Trans",
          "page_text": "Amantya Technologies was founded in 2018 by Anuradha Gupta and Sanjay Bisen and is headquartered in Gurugram, Haryana, India, with offices in Bengaluru, Nagpur, the United States, the United Kingdom, and Canada. The company is privately held and operates as a product engineering and systems integration firm specializing in 5G, IoT, AI, edge computing, and cloud solutions. Amantya has expanded into GCC enablement services, offering AI-powered Global Capability Center solutions that combine pre-trained talent, AI-enabled accelerators, and end-to-end engineering services. The company GCC framework is built on intelligent automation, orchestration, and AI agent-driven delivery. Amantya offers three engagement models for GCCs: Build-Operate-Transfer where the company designs staffs and operates the GCC end-to-end before transitioning to full client ownership; Managed Services where Amantya takes full ownership of defined functions combining AI accelerators and expert squads; and Staff Augmentation providing skilled engineers and domain experts on demand. The company AI solutions include AI Code Transformation, AI Log Analyzer, Autonomous Network Suite, and DevOps and Infrastructure AI. Amantya serves tier-1 operators, enterprises, OEMs, and system integrators across telecommunications, technology, and manufacturing industries. The company employs approximately 558 to 746 people globally with the majority based in India. Annual revenue is estimated between 50 million and 100 million dollars with the Indian entity reporting 124 crore Indian rupees for the fiscal year ending March 2024. Amantya has received the Bharat Telecom Export Excellence Award 2025, Globalisation Excellence Award 2025, and Best AI for Telecommunications at the Entrepreneur India AI Awards Summit 2025. Leadership is headed by Founder and CEO Anuradha Gupta with Co-founder and CTO Sanjay Bisen.\nAlgomine was founded in 2015 and is headquartered in Warsaw, Mazowieckie, Poland. The company is part of Trans",
