          "excerpt": "UAE tops global AI adoption with 𝟱𝟵.𝟰% of workforce using AI tools! | Carrington Malin\nAgree & Join LinkedIn\nBy clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s\nUser Agreement\n,\nPrivacy Policy\n, and\nCookie Policy\n.\nSkip to main content\nLinkedIn\nTop Content\nPeople\nLearning\nJobs\nGames\nSign in\nJoin now\nUAE leads global AI adoption with 59.4% workforce using AI tools\nThis title was summarized by AI from the post below.\nCarrington Malin\nCarrington Malin is an Influencer\n11mo\nEdited\nReport this post\nUAE tops global AI adoption with 𝟱𝟵.𝟰% of workforce using AI tools!\n\nThe\n#UAE\nnow leads the world in artificial intelligence adoption, with 𝟱𝟵.𝟰% of its working-age population using AI tools daily, according to\nMicrosoft\n’s \n𝗔𝗜 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝗚𝗼𝗼𝗱 𝗟𝗮𝗯. The new 𝗔𝗜 𝗗𝗶𝗳𝗳𝘂𝘀𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗥𝗲𝗽𝗼𝗿𝘁 credits the UAE’s coordinated digital policy, infrastructure and education investments as key success factors.\n\nThis milestone positions the UAE as a model for AI-driven digital transformation, showing that policy alignment and readiness can rival even the biggest technology markets. \n\n🡆 🡆 𝗥𝗘𝗔𝗗 the full story on 𝗠𝗶𝗱𝗱𝗹𝗲 𝗘𝗮𝘀𝘁 𝗔𝗜 𝗡𝗲𝘄𝘀\nhttps://lnkd.in/ehAJZFa7\n👉\nMicrosoft\n’s 𝗔𝗜 𝗗𝗶𝗳𝗳𝘂𝘀𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗥𝗲𝗽𝗼𝗿𝘁 ranks the UAE 1st globally with 59.4% AI adoption, followed by Singapore (58.6%), Norway and Ireland.\n\n👉 Over 1.2 billion people worldwide now use AI tools, making it the fastest-spreading technology in history.\n\n👉 Other regional figures: Qatar 35.7%, Saudi Arabia 23.7%, Kuwait 17.7%, Egypt 12.5%, showing a strong UAE lead",
          "page_text": "UAE tops global AI adoption with 𝟱𝟵.𝟰% of workforce using AI tools! | Carrington Malin\nAgree & Join LinkedIn\nBy clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s\nUser Agreement\n,\nPrivacy Policy\n, and\nCookie Policy\n.\nSkip to main content\nLinkedIn\nTop Content\nPeople\nLearning\nJobs\nGames\nSign in\nJoin now\nUAE leads global AI adoption with 59.4% workforce using AI tools\nThis title was summarized by AI from the post below.\nCarrington Malin\nCarrington Malin is an Influencer\n11mo\nEdited\nReport this post\nUAE tops global AI adoption with 𝟱𝟵.𝟰% of workforce using AI tools!\n\nThe\n#UAE\nnow leads the world in artificial intelligence adoption, with 𝟱𝟵.𝟰% of its working-age population using AI tools daily, according to\nMicrosoft\n’s \n𝗔𝗜 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝗚𝗼𝗼𝗱 𝗟𝗮𝗯. The new 𝗔𝗜 𝗗𝗶𝗳𝗳𝘂𝘀𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗥𝗲𝗽𝗼𝗿𝘁 credits the UAE’s coordinated digital policy, infrastructure and education investments as key success factors.\n\nThis milestone positions the UAE as a model for AI-driven digital transformation, showing that policy alignment and readiness can rival even the biggest technology markets. \n\n🡆 🡆 𝗥𝗘𝗔𝗗 the full story on 𝗠𝗶𝗱𝗱𝗹𝗲 𝗘𝗮𝘀𝘁 𝗔𝗜 𝗡𝗲𝘄𝘀\nhttps://lnkd.in/ehAJZFa7\n👉\nMicrosoft\n’s 𝗔𝗜 𝗗𝗶𝗳𝗳𝘂𝘀𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗥𝗲𝗽𝗼𝗿𝘁 ranks the UAE 1st globally with 59.4% AI adoption, followed by Singapore (58.6%), Norway and Ireland.\n\n👉 Over 1.2 billion people worldwide now use AI tools, making it the fastest-spreading technology in history.\n\n👉 Other regional figures: Qatar 35.7%, Saudi Arabia 23.7%, Kuwait 17.7%, Egypt 12.5%, showing a strong UAE lead.\n\n𝘞𝘢𝘯𝘵 𝘵𝘰 𝘴𝘦𝘦 𝘈𝘓𝘓 𝘮𝘺 𝘧𝘶𝘵𝘶𝘳𝘦 𝘱𝘰𝘴𝘵𝘴? 𝘊𝘭𝘪𝘤𝘬 🔔 𝘰𝘯 𝘮𝘺 𝘱𝘳𝘰𝘧𝘪𝘭𝘦 𝘱𝘢𝘨𝘦.\n\nSubscribe to the weekly 𝗠𝗶𝗱𝗱𝗹𝗲 𝗘𝗮𝘀𝘁 𝗔𝗜 𝗡𝗲𝘄𝘀 email news digest:\nhttps://bit.ly/4fViAVP\nSubscribe to the weekly 𝗔𝗳𝗿𝗶𝗰𝗮 𝗔𝗜 𝗡𝗲𝘄𝘀 email news digest:\nhttps://lnkd.in/dfkbFeVz\nSubscribe to my monthly 𝗔𝗜 𝗙𝗶𝗿𝘀𝘁 marketing newsletter:\nhttps://lnkd.in/daxbKnJh\n#MiddleEastAINews\n[ 𝖳𝖾𝗑𝗍 50% AI Created | 50% 𝖧𝗎𝗆𝖺𝗇 𝖢𝗋𝖾𝖺𝗍𝖾𝖽 | Image credit: Microsoft AI for Good AI Diffusion Report]\n35\n3 Comments\nLike\nComment\nShare\nCopy\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nX\nMohamed ElBendary, PhD\n11mo\nReport this comment\nThanks for sharing\nCarrington Malin\n! The data is great to see. IMHO, while I am not an expert on UAE's tech scene, this data is not a surprise. The announcements consistently point to the UAE building systemic AI capabilities covering the entire AI capability stack: local compute with diversified supply chain, talent pipeline investments, horizontal and vertical use cases investments across sectors, regulatory agility to avoid uncertainty tax on innovation, digital transformation of existing value chains to hydrate AI with clean data infrastructure, and probably more that I have not seen yet, all pointing to intentional strategic design. It is literally exhilarating to see.\nLike\nReply\n1 Reaction\n2 Reactions\nBassam Hajj\n11mo\nReport this comment\nRemarkable validation of the UAE’s forward-thinking strategy, where investment in digital policy, education, and infrastructure converges to create real-world AI readiness. The results speak for themselves, and the momentum is only growing 👏\nLike\nReply\n1 Reaction\n2 Reactions\nSee more comments\nTo view or add a comment,\nsign in\n36,928 followers\n3000+ Posts\n291 Articles\nView Profile\nFollow\nMore from this author\nSaudi AI registrations up 31%; and more Middle East AI News\nCarrington Malin\n1d\nFalcon-Emirati LLM launched; and more Middle East AI News\nCarrington Malin\n1w\nUAE biz AI use jumps to 72%; and more Middle East AI News\nCarrington Malin\n2w\nExplore related topics\nHow AI Coding Tools Drive Rapid Adoption\nAI Adoption Strategies for the Modern Workforce\nInnovations Driving AI Adoption in Enterprises\nKey Benefits of AI Adoption\nLatest Trends in Government AI Adoption\nHow to Drive AI Adoption\nBest Practices for AI Adoption\nHow to Drive Companywide Adoption of AI Tools\nHow AI Adoption Drives Cloud Provider Revenue\nAI adoption in insurance since 2015\nShow more\n