          "page_text": "uae Artificial Intelligence (AI) Market Size, Share,Trends, Growth Analysis Report, 2031\nHome\nInformation and Communications Technology\nArtificial Intelligence (AI) Market\nUAE\nUAE Artificial Intelligence (AI) Market (2026-2031)\nReport Code\nTC 7894 UAE\nPublished in\nJul 2026, By MarketsandMarkets™\nChoose License Type\nSINGLE USER $ 2950\nCORPORATE LICENSE $ 3400\nInquire Before Buying\nOverview\nRequest Sample Pages\nRequest Customization\nDownload PDF\nYou are viewing:\nUAE Artificial Intelligence (AI) Market analysis\nPart of:\nArtificial Intelligence (AI) Market\n(Global)\nThe UAE Artificial Intelligence (AI) Market was valued at\n$1786.7  Million in 2026\nand projected to reach to\n$11249.9  Million by 2031\n, representing a compound annual growth rate of\nCAGR\n30.1%\n.\nThe UAE artificial intelligence market is poised for exceptional growth through 2031, driven by strategic government initiatives, substantial public and private sector investments, and the nation's commitment to becoming a global AI leader.\nUAE Artificial Intelligence (AI) Market (2026-2031)  : Size and Share\nCAGR of\nUSD Million\nMARKET SNAPSHOT\nMarket Size in\nUSD 26.32 MN\nMarket Forecast in\nCAGR\nForecast Period\nUnits Considered\nValue (USD MN)\nUAE Artificial Intelligence (AI) Market Trends and Insights\nThe UAE's strategic positioning as a regional technology hub, combined with substantial government investment in digital transformation and smart city initiatives, is driving accelerated AI adoption across sectors.\nThe UAE's\n30.1%\ncompound annual growth rate significantly outpaces global trends, reflecting the nation's commitment to becoming a global AI leader.\n\nThe UAE market is characterized by strong enterprise demand for AI-powered solutions in healthcare, finance, retail, and government services.\nThe UAE's regulatory framework and innovation-friendly ecosystem are attracting both domestic and international AI vendors, fostering competitive market dynamics.\nBy 2031, the UAE is positioned to capture substantial value within the Middle East and Africa region, driven by increasing cloud adoption, data analytics capabilities, and automation investments across public and private sectors..\nKey Market Statistics\nCAGR (2026-2031)\nCAGR 30.1%\nMarket Size, 2026\n~USD 1786.7  Million\nForecast, 2031\n~USD 11249.9  Million\nCountry\nUAE\nUAE Artificial Intelligence (AI) Market Overview\nExplosive Growth Trajectory :\nUAE's AI market is projected to grow from USD 1,786.7 million in 2026 to USD 11,249.9 million by 2031, representing a robust 30.1% CAGR, outpacing the global average of 29.3%.\nGovernment-Driven Digital Transformation :\nThe UAE government's strategic investments in smart city initiatives, digital infrastructure, and AI adoption policies are creating a favorable ecosystem for rapid market expansion and innovation.\nRegional Technology Hub Status :\nDubai and Abu Dhabi's positioning as Middle East technology leaders attract multinational AI companies, startups, and venture capital, establishing the UAE as a critical regional innovation center.\nCross-Sector AI Integration :\nAI adoption is accelerating across UAE's key sectors including healthcare, finance, retail, logistics, and government services, driven by digital transformation mandates and competitive pressures.\nUAE Artificial Intelligence (AI) Market Dynamics\nThe UAE's Vision 2031 framework and digital transformation roadmaps are catalyzing widespread AI adoption across healthcare, financial services, smart cities, and e-commerce sectors.\nWith a\n30.1%\nCAGR significantly exceeding global benchmarks, the market reflects strong demand for AI-powered solutions in automation, data analytics, and intelligent systems.\nContinued government support, regulatory frameworks favoring innovation, and the influx of international tech talent position the UAE as the fastest-growing AI market in the Middle East region..\nMarket Ecosystem\nARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE (AI) MARKET: COMMERCIAL USE CASES ACROSS INDUSTRIES\nCOMPANY\nUSE CASE DESCRIPTION\nBENEFITS\nKlarna deployed an OpenAI-powered AI assistant across its customer service operations, covering 23 markets and over 35 languages | The platform replaced a large share of first-line support interactions, routing complex cases to human agents\nHandled 2.3 million conversations in the first month | Automated 67% of all customer service chats, equivalent to the output of 700 full-time agents | Average resolution time dropped from 11 minutes to under 2 minutes | Repeat inquiries fell 25%\nTreviPay implemented Tricentis Testim, an AI-powered UI test automation tool, to support cloud migration of 25+ applications and to scale regression coverage across multiple Agile teams\nAI models assessed more than 5,000 daily shipments from plants to warehouses, generating over USD 20 million in savings since fiscal 2024 | Real-time manufacturing performance data is projected to deliver more than USD 50 million in waste reduction\nMeta built one of the world's largest AI compute infrastructures, deploying tens of thousands of NVIDIA H100 GPUs across purpose-built data center clusters to train and serve its large language models, including the Llama series\nHardware foundation enabled Meta to release Llama models as open-source, accelerating AI research and product development across industries\nInsilico Medicine used its end-to-end generative AI platform to identify a novel drug target for idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis (IPF) and develop a candidate molecule entirely through AI-driven design, from target discovery through to clinical development\nAdvanced from novel target identification to Phase I clinical trial in under 30 months — approximately half the traditional timeline\nDell Technologies deployed its AI Factory with NVIDIA, an end-to-end AI infrastructure and services platform, to help enterprises move AI initiatives from pilot to production | The offering integrates AI-ready data platforms, scalable hardware, and implementation services\nOver 4,000 enterprise customers deployed the Dell AI Factory within two years of launch | Early adopters reported up to 2.6x ROI within the first year of deployment\nLogos and trademarks shown above are the property of their respective owners. Their use here is for informational and illustrative purposes only.\nRelated Ecosystem\nKey Takeaways\nThe UAE AI market will grow from USD 1,786.7M (2026) to USD 11,249.9M (2031), representing a 30.1% CAGR.\nThe UAE's government-led digital transformation initiatives and smart city projects are primary growth catalysts for AI adoption.\nThe UAE attracts significant foreign investment and talent in AI, positioning it as the regional innovation leader.\nEnterprise demand in the UAE across healthcare, finance, and government sectors is driving robust AI solution deployment.\nArtificial Intelligence (AI) Market Report Scope\nReport Metric\nDetails\nBase Year\n2026\nFastest Growing Segment\nMULTI-AGENT ORCHESTRATION PLATFORMS (Ai Agent Orchestration & Rag Platform)\nForecast Period\n2026–2031\nGrowth Rate\nCAGR of 29.3% from 2026 to 2031\nLargest Segment\nENTERPRISES (End User)\nMarket Size Base Year (Billions)\n~USD  602.12 (2026)\nRevenue Forecast (Billions)\n~USD  2176.08 (2031)\nSegments Covered\nOffering, Hardware, Business Function, Marketing & Sales, Human Resources, Finance & Accounting, Operations & Supply Chain, Cybersecurity, Bfsi Use Case, Retail & Ecommerce Use Case, Manufacturing Use Case, Government & Defense Use Case, Healthcare & Life Sciences Use Case, Healthcare & Life Science Use Case, Telecommunications Use Case, Energy & Utilities Use Case, Transportation & Logistics Use Case, Agriculture Use Case, Software & Technology Providers Use Case, Media & Entertainment Use Case, End User, Enterprise Ai, Bfsi End User, Manufacturing End User, Government & Defense End User, Healthcare & Life Sciences End User, Energy & Utilities End User, Ai Accelerator Chi