          "excerpt": "2026 UN Water Conference | Department of Economic and Social Affairs\nSorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website.\nSkip to main content\nWelcome to the United Nations\nعربي\n中文\nEnglish\nFrançais\nРусский\nEspañol\nUNITED NATIONS WATER CONFERENCE\nABU DHABI 2026\nPrimary navigation\nHome\nAbout\nProgramme\nEvents\nSide Events\nParticipate\nParticipate\nAttending the Conference\nDocumentation\nPreparatory Process\nPGA meeting and multistakeholder events\nOrganizational Session\nInteractive Dialogues\nStakeholders\nMedia\n8 - 10 December 2026\nAbu Dhabi National Exhibition Centre (ADNEC)\nAbu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates\nAchieving Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) 6 on Clean Water and\n        Sanitation is an essential end in itself and is also critical to progress\n        on the 2030 Agenda as a whole. As we enter the final 5 years of the 2030\n        Agenda and its SDGs, the world must surge investment, innovation and\n        political will towards the accelerated implementation of SDG 6 in a\n        spirit of solidarity and cooperation.\nThe 2026 United Nations Water Conference, co-hosted by the United Arab\n        Emirates and Senegal, and convened in UAE 8-10 December 2026, will bring\n        this spirit of solidarity to life and help to build a water-secure future\n        for all.\nSign up for conference updates →\n|\nQuestions?\nwater2026@un.org\nAbout the Conference\n→\nRegistration\n→\nHost Country Requirements\n→\nProgramme\n→\nResources for Stakeholders\n→\nResources for Media\n→\nLatest Updates\nRe",
          "page_text": "2026 UN Water Conference | Department of Economic and Social Affairs\nSorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website.\nSkip to main content\nWelcome to the United Nations\nعربي\n中文\nEnglish\nFrançais\nРусский\nEspañol\nUNITED NATIONS WATER CONFERENCE\nABU DHABI 2026\nPrimary navigation\nHome\nAbout\nProgramme\nEvents\nSide Events\nParticipate\nParticipate\nAttending the Conference\nDocumentation\nPreparatory Process\nPGA meeting and multistakeholder events\nOrganizational Session\nInteractive Dialogues\nStakeholders\nMedia\n8 - 10 December 2026\nAbu Dhabi National Exhibition Centre (ADNEC)\nAbu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates\nAchieving Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) 6 on Clean Water and\n        Sanitation is an essential end in itself and is also critical to progress\n        on the 2030 Agenda as a whole. As we enter the final 5 years of the 2030\n        Agenda and its SDGs, the world must surge investment, innovation and\n        political will towards the accelerated implementation of SDG 6 in a\n        spirit of solidarity and cooperation.\nThe 2026 United Nations Water Conference, co-hosted by the United Arab\n        Emirates and Senegal, and convened in UAE 8-10 December 2026, will bring\n        this spirit of solidarity to life and help to build a water-secure future\n        for all.\nSign up for conference updates →\n|\nQuestions?\nwater2026@un.org\nAbout the Conference\n→\nRegistration\n→\nHost Country Requirements\n→\nProgramme\n→\nResources for Stakeholders\n→\nResources for Media\n→\nLatest Updates\nRegistration open for all categories of participants\n→\nConcept Papers for the Six Interactive Dialogue themes released!\n→\nUN system registration now open (deadline 13 November 2026)\n→\nRegistration for Accredited Stakeholders\n        (deadline 6 November 2026, 23:59 EDT)\n→\nOpen Call for Virtual Side Events\n        (deadline 16 October 2026)\n→\nInteractive Dialogues\nAs per General Assembly Resolution\nA/RES/78/327\n,\n\n      the 2026 UN Water Conference will include six interactive dialogues,\n\n      to be held in parallel with the plenary meetings. Summaries of the\n\n      interactive dialogues should be presented to the Conference at its\n\n      closing plenary meeting, followed by a written submission for the\n\n      final report of the Conference.\n8 December 2026\n8 December 2026\n9 December 2026\n9 December 2026\n10 December 2026\n10 December 2026\nJoin the conversation:\nFooter menu\nContact\nCopyright\nFraud Alert\nPrivacy Notice\nTerms of Use",
