          "excerpt": "Share Of Voice - Political Social Listening For Progressives\n0\nSkip to Content\nAbout\nFAQs\nSubstack/Podcast\nBook A Consultation\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nAbout\nFAQs\nSubstack/Podcast\nBook A Consultation\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nAbout\nFAQs\nSubstack/Podcast\nBook A Consultation\nYOUR\nWINNING\nMESSAGE\nIS OUT THERE.\nARE YOU\nLISTENING?\nShare Of Voice identifies\nstrategic and messaging insights\nfor progressive causes by taking a listen-first approach studying patterns emerging from\nmillions of online voices\ntalking on public social media about the\ntopics that are important\nto them.\nBook a Consultation\nREPORTING HIGHLIGHTS\nFindings that were significant enough to be featured in one of our newsletters.\nREAD MORE\nREAD MORE\nREAD MORE\nBEFORE YOU\nSPEAK\n,\nLISTEN\nShare Of Voice can help your organization\nbetter understand\n:\nWHAT\nMATTERS MOST?\nUnderstand what’s\nmost important to the audience\nyou’re trying to connect with.\nWhat are people talking about online, and what narratives are they absorbing on social media? Does your issue focus match what real people discussing with their friends and acquaintances online?\nWHO\nIS SHARING THEIR VOICE?\nTarget the\nconstituencies who care the most\nabout your priorities.\nShare Of Voice can show you who is participating in online conversations - age groups, gender distribution, demographic subgroup participation (parents, veterans, etc.), and much more. (And we can work backwards, listening to a specific audience and learning what’s most important to them.)\nHOW\nDO PEOPL",
          "page_text": "Share Of Voice - Political Social Listening For Progressives\n0\nSkip to Content\nAbout\nFAQs\nSubstack/Podcast\nBook A Consultation\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nAbout\nFAQs\nSubstack/Podcast\nBook A Consultation\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nAbout\nFAQs\nSubstack/Podcast\nBook A Consultation\nYOUR\nWINNING\nMESSAGE\nIS OUT THERE.\nARE YOU\nLISTENING?\nShare Of Voice identifies\nstrategic and messaging insights\nfor progressive causes by taking a listen-first approach studying patterns emerging from\nmillions of online voices\ntalking on public social media about the\ntopics that are important\nto them.\nBook a Consultation\nREPORTING HIGHLIGHTS\nFindings that were significant enough to be featured in one of our newsletters.\nREAD MORE\nREAD MORE\nREAD MORE\nBEFORE YOU\nSPEAK\n,\nLISTEN\nShare Of Voice can help your organization\nbetter understand\n:\nWHAT\nMATTERS MOST?\nUnderstand what’s\nmost important to the audience\nyou’re trying to connect with.\nWhat are people talking about online, and what narratives are they absorbing on social media? Does your issue focus match what real people discussing with their friends and acquaintances online?\nWHO\nIS SHARING THEIR VOICE?\nTarget the\nconstituencies who care the most\nabout your priorities.\nShare Of Voice can show you who is participating in online conversations - age groups, gender distribution, demographic subgroup participation (parents, veterans, etc.), and much more. (And we can work backwards, listening to a specific audience and learning what’s most important to them.)\nHOW\nDO PEOPLE SHARE THEIR VOICE?\nSpeak to people\nusing language that they already use\nthemselves.\nPoliticians and organizations often use rhetoric that doesn’t quite connect - Share Of Voice can help you find out how real people talk about the issues, so that your messaging can meet the moment.\nWHY\nSHARE OF VOICE IS THE TOOL FOR YOU\nPolls aren’t telling\nthe whole story\n.\nOnly 1 in 15 Americans responds to pollsters (Source: Niskansen Center, 2022). Share Of Voice can\nidentify those surges of passion and emotion\namong key voter groups in realtime, before they show up in polls - such as when more people mentioned President Biden the day after his first debate with Trump than on any other day of his Presidency (see left image).\nWhat matters\ntoday is not what mattered yesterday.\nYour organization can’t afford to waste resources on an issue that’s fading in importance. Share Of Voice monitors conversations as they evolve and can capture reactions to major events in realtime, so you know\nwhat matters most right now\nto the people you’re trying to reach. (Pictured at left - a month-over-month increase in the number of social media posts in Arizona talking about high housing costs.)\nIdentify\nharmful narratives\nas they emerge.\nDon’t let your campaign or organization be capsized by a harmful narrative online - Share Of Voice can\nidentify and monitor disinformation, misinformation, and other online narrative threats\nto your mission and message. If a harmful narrative is detected, we can show you how large or small it is, whether it’s growing or declining, and help your organization discover the most effective counter-messaging so you know how to fight back. (Pictured at left - a late surge in advocacy for a “No” vote on Ohio’s Issue 1 in 2024.)\nCONTACT US.\nRead Newsletter\nBook a Consultation",
