                                          2-for-1 stock splits on April 7, 2006, \n                                                                                    2-for-1 stock splits on September 12, 2001, and \n                                                                                    2-for-1 stock splits on June 27, 2000.\nStock splits do not change NVIDIA Corporation’s total market value,\n                                    but they increase the number of shares outstanding and reduce the per-share price,\n                                    making the stock more accessible to investors.\nLearn more about NVIDIA Corporation's\nRevenue\n,\nCEO Salary\n,\nEmployees\nand\nRevenue by Segment\n.\nCheck out\ncompetitors\n.\nExplore additional\nfinancial\nmetrics (e.g.,\nMarket Cap\n).\n...more\nRead less\nNVIDIA Corporation has a market cap of\n$$5.35 Trillion\n(as of Oct 14, 2026), making it the world's\n# 1\nlargest company by market cap.\nContinue Reading...\nMarket Capitalization, often referred to as \"Market Cap\" is the total value of a company's outstanding shares. It is calculated by multiplying the company's current share price by the total number of shares outstanding. Market cap is a quick measure of a company's size and market value.\nLearn more about NVIDIA Corporation's\nRevenue\n,\nCEO Salary\n,\nEmployees\nand\nRevenue by Segment\n.\nCheck out\ncompetitors\nto\n                                            NVIDIA Corporation in\n                                            a side-by-side comparison.\nExplore additional\nfinancial\n                                            metrics\nfor NVIDIA Corporation.\nRead less\nStock Price\nMarket Cap\nPE Ratio\nStock Split\nDividend\nStock Price\n$198.3 B\nFY, 2022\nMarket cap\n$0 B\nFY, 2022\nDividends\n$0\nFY, 2022\nPE Ratio\n$198.3 B\nFY, 2022\nShares Outsanding\n$198.3 B\nFY, 2022\nMarket Capitalization\n$198.3 B\nFY, 2022\nNVIDIA Corporation Stock Split: History & Recent Updates\nLast Updated: 