oss Reddit and other forums are positive. That is roughly in line with its 30-day average.\nThe score is a real-time read on how the retail crowd feels about the stock. It is not a price forecast on its own, but a sustained shift in sentiment often accompanies changing momentum.\nHow Intel Sentiment Compares to Peers\nAt 71/100, Intel has stronger investor sentiment than AMD (68/100), but weaker than NVIDIA (74/100). All three are Semiconductor names, so the read reflects how the retail crowd feels about Intel relative to its direct competitors.\nHow We Calculate Intel’s Sentiment Score\nAltIndex calculates Intel’s sentiment with natural language processing (NLP): it parses investor posts from Reddit, Stocktwits, and other investing forums, assesses the tone, keywords, and context of each mention, and classifies it as positive, neutral, or negative. Those are aggregated into a single 0–100 score (0 = most bearish, 100 = most bullish). Unlike trackers that simply count article mentions or tally blogger ratings, this reads the actual language of retail-investor discussion.\nSentiment is one of 25+ alternative data signals in the\nINTC AI Score\n(currently 64/100). For the platform-level activity behind it, see INTC\nReddit mentions\n,\nStocktwits mentions\n, and\nX mentions\n— plus\nnews coverage\n. To see which stocks the retail crowd is most bullish on, view the\nmost-discussed stocks on Reddit\n.\nStay ahead on INTC\nTrack Intel’s investor sentiment and 25+ alternative data signals\nGet notified when sentiment on INTC flips bullish or bearish — alongside Reddit, Stocktwits, and news.\nGet Started for FREE\nMonth over Month\nSentiment\nSep 2026\n72\n2.2%\nAug 2026\n70\n2.3%\nJul 2026\n68\n5.5%\nJun 2026\n72\n3%\nMay 2026\n70\n0.3%\nApr 2026\n70\n1.4%\nGet INTC alerts in real-time\nThe moment the sentiment trend turns, sentiment flips, or insiders trade.\nTry Stock Alerts Free\nIntel Sentiment: Frequently Asked Questions\nWhat is the current sentiment for INTC?\nIntel’s sentiment score is 71/100, which is bullish. The score is based on NLP analysis of investor discussions across Reddit, Stocktwits, and other investing forums, updated daily.\nIs INTC bullish or bearish right now?\nBased on social-media sentiment analysis, Intel is currently leaning bullish, with a majority of investor discussions positive. Sentiment is one of 25+ signals in the\nINTC AI Score\n(64/100).\nAnalyzing Sentiment, how is Intel performing compared to its industry peers?\nIntel overperforms a majority of its industry peers when it comes to Sentiment, ranking in the 70th percentile.\nHow does AltIndex calculate sentiment for Intel?\nAltIndex calculates sentiment for Intel by analyzing posts from various internet stock forums, including Reddit. We employ advanced natural language processing techniques to parse and understand the context of each post. Our algorithm assesses the tone, keywords, and overall context of mentions to determine whether they are positive, neutral, or negative. The sentiment from all posts is then aggregated into a score ranging from 0 to 100. A higher score indicates that a majority of the mentions are positive or bullish, while a lower score signifies that the majority of mentions are negative or bearish. This comprehensive analysis allows us to provide an estimated sentiment score that reflects the current investor mood towards Intel.\nSign up\nand get more insights on Intel.\nThe analytics provided are estimates and not a substitute for professional advice. All investments involve risks, including possible capital loss.\n×\nUnlock full history\nSee Intel’s complete sentiment history\nSign up to unlock 1-year and all-time charts for INTC, plus 25+ alternative data signals, AI Scores, and real-time alerts.\nGet Started for FREE\nAbout AltIndex\nSmarter investing with alternative data analytics and AI-powered insights.\nNewsletter\nAI stock picks and market insights, straight to your inbox.\nSubscribe on our newsletter page →\nCom