ns in enterprise and data center networking, including artificial intelligence networking and connectivity, home connectivity, set-top boxes, broadband access, telecommunication equipment, wireless device and base stations, data center servers and storage systems, factory automation, power generation and alternative energy systems, and electronic displays. Broadcom Inc. was founded in 1961 and is headquartered in Palo Alto, California.\nwww.broadcom.com\n33,000\nFull Time Employees\nNovember 02\nFiscal Year Ends\nTechnology\nSector\nSemiconductors\nIndustry\nMore about Broadcom Inc.\nRecent News\nView More\nAll\nNews\nEarnings Calls\nPress Releases\nSEC Filings\nView More\nPerformance Overview\nTrailing total returns as of 10/16/2026, which may include dividends or other distributions.\nBenchmark is\nS&P 500 (^GSPC)\n.\nYTD Return\nAVGO\n3.09%\nS&P 500 (^GSPC)\n12.35%\n1-Year Return\nAVGO\n5.11%\nS&P 500 (^GSPC)\n16.01%\n3-Year Return\nAVGO\n281.76%\nS&P 500 (^GSPC)\n75.84%\n5-Year Return\nAVGO\n624.07%\nS&P 500 (^GSPC)\n72.00%\nEarnings Trends\nView More\nEarnings Per Share\ngaap\nGAAP\nnongaap\nNormalized\ngaap\nGAAP\nnongaap\nNormalized\nRevenue vs. Earnings\nyearly\nAnnual\nquarterly\nQuarterly\nyearly\nAnnual\nquarterly\nQuarterly\nQ3 FY26\nRevenue\n29.59B\nEarnings\n13.09B\nProfit Margin\n44.23%\nQ4\nFY25\nQ1\nFY26\nQ2\nFY26\nQ3\nFY26\n0\n10B\n20B\n40.0%\n42.0%\n44.0%\n46.0%\nView More\nAnalyst Insights\nView More\nAnalyst Price Targets\n215.88\nLow\n527.59\nAverage\n333.56\nCurrent\n660.00\nHigh\nAnalyst Recommendations\nStrong Buy\nBuy\nHold\nUnderperform\nSell\nLatest Rating\nDate\n9/10/2026\nAnalyst\nPiper Sandler\nRating Action\nInitiated\nRating\nOverweight\nPrice Action\nAnnounces\nPrice Target\n460\nView More\nStatistics\nView More\nValuation Measures\nMarket Cap\nEnterprise Value\nTrailing P/E\nForward P/E\nPEG Ratio (5yr expected)\nPrice/Sales  (ttm)\nPrice/Book  (mrq)\nEnterprise Value/Revenue\nEnterprise Value/EBITDA\nFinancial Highlights\nProfitab